d opioids for neuropathic pain; consider low-dose amitriptyline at bedtime if sleep disruption.\n\n**7. Therapy Goals**:\n- PT: Wheelchair mobility, transfer training (sliding board initially, then depression transfers), strengthening of trunk and UE, standing frame program.\n- OT: ADL independence, wheelchair skills, adaptive equipment training, home modification assessment.\n- Psychology: Adjustment counseling, coping skills, peer mentoring referral.\n\n**8. Autonomic Dysreflexia Education**:\n- Although T6 is at the threshold, educate patient and staff on recognition and emergency management of AD (pounding headache, HTN, flushing/sweating above level, bradycardia). Most common triggers: bladder distension, bowel impaction, skin breakdown.',
